SAR ADC differential split capacitive DAC, x17 (VDN) and x18 (VDP) of the golden deck, ideal capacitors, 1024 codes in one run
* specs/analog/decks/sar_cdac_diff.cir -- test data for specs/analog/sar_cdac.t27 (#10540). A plain netlist, no .control block.
* Two copies of the Diff_cap_DAC topology of sar_cdac_half.cir (see there for the unit counts and the deck lines they come from).
* P half (x18, top plate mp, net1 lp, plates pp1..pp10): sampled at 0.875 V. N half (x17, top plate mn, net1 ln, plates pn1..pn10): sampled at 0.625 V.
* Every plate rests at VCM = 0.75 V until 10 ns. Interval n (n = 0..1023, 10 ns each): P plate j is at VDD = 1.5 V when bit j-1 of n is 1 and at 0 V
* when it is 0; the N plates are the complement (neg_bottom_plate_logic: Bit_n = not Bit once the bit is decided), so the N code is 1023 - n.
* The network is algebraic (capacitors only), so the settled voltage of an interval does not depend on the time grid.
* Read the LAST printed point inside each interval. Run: ngspice -b sar_cdac_diff.cir   (the spec records v(mp) and v(mn) for 16 codes;
* .print shows 7 digits, the spec's values were read with set numdgt=15 in a control block wrapped around this same netlist).
